Done. I combined all 16 converted functions from `.../6/all.R/` (a directory of JSON conversion outputs, despite its `.R`-looking name) into `r2py_kernsmooth/__init__.py`:

**Functions included**: `bkde`, `bkde2D`, `bkfe`, `blkest`, `cpblock`, `dpih`, `dpik`, `dpill`, `linbin`, `linbin2D`, `locpoly`, `rlbin`, `sdiag`, `sstdiag` (matching the existing `__all__`), plus `on_attach`/`on_unload` (R package lifecycle hooks, defined but not exported, matching R's convention of not exposing `.onAttach`/`.onUnload`).

**Key corrections made during integration**:
- **Dropped all self-referential local imports** (`from .linbin import linbin`, `from .bkfe import bkfe`, etc.) — since every function now lives in the same module, these would have caused circular-import errors (there's no `linbin.py`, `bkfe.py`, etc. as separate files).
- **Merged duplicate `scipy.stats` imports** — `bkde` needed `norm, beta` while `bkde2D`/`bkfe` needed just `norm`; combined into one `from scipy.stats import beta, norm`.
- **Preserved the pre-existing `from . import _KernSmooth`** import, since `meson.build` always compiles that extension module as part of the build (none of the ported functions call into it — they're all pure Python/NumPy re-implementations — but removing it wasn't necessary or requested).

I verified the result by `py_compile`-checking it and actually running `bkde`, `linbin`, `dpik`, `dpih`, `bkde2D`, and `dpill` (which exercises the full dependency chain: `rlbin` → `cpblock` → `blkest` → `locpoly` → `sdiag`/`sstdiag`) against synthetic data — all executed correctly.
